# A creature NOT made of stone must take no effect from Soften Stone (inc-wqql,
# step 5). Same session as tools/keys/soften-stone-golem.keys, but a cave orc
# stands east instead of a stone golem. The before/after wizard dumps of the
# orc (pressing W on the aimed creature; src/Term.cpp EffectPrompt) must show
# no armour change, no soften stone stati and no slow stati; the caster's own
# dump must be identical before and after; and the message log must show the
# cast happened (V opens View Messages, src/Tables.cpp) with no "softens"/
# "slows down" text.
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/druid-shoulder-metal-seed7-opt0822.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/soften-stone-orc.keys 1
#
# THE READ. While the "Soften Stone" aim prompt is up (mode 9), the cursor
# starts on the caster himself, so W opens the CASTER's Thing::Dump(); RIGHT
# moves the cursor onto the orc one square east and W opens the ORC's dump.
# The dump prints "A ARM <v> (base ...)" and the Stati list, which is the
# oracle for armour and slow, before and after the cast.
SPACE
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Soften Stone" ENTER
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Orc"
@choose "cave orc"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:summoned
@until "HP:" ESC

# BEFORE: start the cast. The cursor starts on the caster, so dump the player
# first, then RIGHT and dump the orc.
@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Soften Stone"
@dump:cast-aim
w
@dump:before-player
DOWN*30
@dump:before-player-stati
ESC
RIGHT
@dump:cast-on-orc
w
@dump:before-orc
DOWN*30
@dump:before-orc-stati

# CAST: ESC closes the wizard dump (still aiming at the orc); ENTER takes the
# creature under the cursor and fires the spell.
ESC
@dump:cast-back
ENTER
@dump:cast-enter
@until "HP:" ESC

# AFTER: aim again; dump the player (cursor on self), then the orc.
@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Soften Stone"
@dump:cast-aim2
w
@dump:after-player
DOWN*30
@dump:after-player-stati
ESC
RIGHT
w
@dump:after-orc
DOWN*30
@dump:after-orc-stati
# ESC closes the wizard dump, leaving the cast aim prompt still up; a second
# ESC cancels the cast and returns to the map, where V opens the message log.
ESC
ESC
@dump:map-back
v
@dump:msglog
ESC
@quit
